Brief description:

This is an one attempted answer to the problem of a "boring gehennom"
-- I have cut the number of levels while increasing the placed object
count and made the monsters a touch more difficult.

1. An ALPHA-level patch without documentation or standards adherence. I
will need a list of the standards in order to ensure the patch is up to
spec.

2. Cuts Gehennom down to approximately 15 levels while increasing
monster difficulty.  Of the 15 levels,  only 3 or so are "filler" --
the rest are the usual named levels plus one additional stolen from
slash'em.

Specific things in need of testing:

1.  Although I did not change the Vibrating Square code, for obvious
reasons I have not walked all over the dungeon to ensure that it always
shows up.  I don't know any reason why it should break,  but assumption
is the mother of all disaster :).

2.  I have eliminated the ability to gate in certain types of demon,
for reasons that will become clear. Again, I was not able to test it
thoroughly to determine that it would NEVER happen.  Even if I had, how
does one prove a negative?

